WEBVTT

00:00.790 --> 00:04.150
<i>A single invitation was delivered to me.</i>

00:03.480 --> 00:05.190
<i><b>Shooting Star Viewing</b></i>

00:04.540 --> 00:06.010
<i>Following it,</i>

00:06.010 --> 00:09.700
<i>Ron and I headed to a certain 
observatory on a remote island.</i>

00:09.740 --> 00:14.870
<b>At the Observatory: 7 People Die Tragically by Gunfire</b>

00:10.020 --> 00:14.870
<i>A horrific mass murder had
 taken place there a decade prior.</i>

00:15.740 --> 00:19.870
<i>And this would mark the first Leonid 
meteor shower viewing party since.</i>

00:19.870 --> 00:23.090
It's a replica. 
The gun wards off evil spirits.

00:24.160 --> 00:25.130
Oh, Director.

00:25.490 --> 00:27.510
What's all the commotion?

00:27.510 --> 00:29.510
I'm Onodera, a photographer 
of celestial objects.

00:29.510 --> 00:31.430
Instructor John Grizzly.

00:31.430 --> 00:33.510
I'm the idol of the constellation Orion...

00:33.930 --> 00:35.310
Orihime, star!

00:35.650 --> 00:39.820
<i>The viewing party was supposed to help 
overcome the tragedy of the past,</i>

00:40.430 --> 00:45.380
<i>but contrary to the director's hopes, 
more killing began to unfold.</i>

00:45.940 --> 00:47.560
<i>The first victim was Onodera-shi,</i>

00:47.560 --> 00:50.060
<i>a woman specializing
 in celestial photography.</i>

00:50.520 --> 00:53.530
<i>She was shot dead in the dome, 
which was locked at the time.</i>

00:53.970 --> 00:55.790
Who exactly are you to him?

00:56.390 --> 00:58.000
He's...

00:58.610 --> 01:01.420
Ron is... my friend.

01:02.080 --> 01:04.900
A friend who would trust him against all logic

01:04.900 --> 01:07.250
is one thing I thought he'd never have.

01:08.140 --> 01:12.550
<i>The second victim was security
 personnel the director had invited.</i>

01:12.550 --> 01:16.350
<i>It was John Grizzly-shi, an instructor 
at the prestigious BLUE academy.</i>

01:17.010 --> 01:19.600
<i>He was shot on the roof of the observatory</i>

01:19.600 --> 01:21.580
<i>and from there, fell to the ground below.</i>

01:21.560 --> 01:27.020
<b>BLUE's Closed Circle Instructor
John Grizzly</b>

01:21.560 --> 01:27.020
<b>Celestial Photographer
Onodera Kayoko</b>

01:22.250 --> 01:24.390
<i>This unending string of murders...</i>

01:23.600 --> 01:27.020
<b>Kamonohashi Ron</b>

01:23.770 --> 01:27.020
<b>Observatory Director
Jumonji Takumi</b>

01:23.850 --> 01:27.020
<b>Astronomy Club Chair
Donzawa Eisaku</b>

01:23.980 --> 01:27.020
<b>Metropolitan Police Detective
 Isshiki Totomaru</b>

01:24.110 --> 01:27.020
<b>Observatory Chef
Unno Minami</b>

01:24.230 --> 01:27.020
<b>Constellation Idol
Orihime</b>

01:24.890 --> 01:27.020
<i>Who could the culprit be?</i>

01:27.020 --> 01:29.470
This island really is cursed!

01:29.470 --> 01:32.990
All of us are going to be found as corpses!

01:32.990 --> 01:34.450
That won't happen.

01:36.210 --> 01:39.250
Despite how he appears, 
Detective Isshiki is enraged.

01:39.670 --> 01:43.320
He loves mysteries more than anyone, 
and he's good at solving them.

01:43.320 --> 01:47.710
But he fell into this trap, and two people 
have been killed right in front of him—

01:48.110 --> 01:51.050
one of them a great sleuth 
worthy of his utmost respect.

01:51.460 --> 01:55.250
The culprit is here, blending in 
with you in your fright.

01:55.250 --> 01:59.870
Beneath their mask, twisted with false fear, 
they must be smiling with triumph.

02:00.940 --> 02:03.370
But they'll regret that.

02:04.240 --> 02:08.160
You have angered someone 
whom you never should have.

02:21.220 --> 02:24.540
Ron    Kamonohashi's

02:21.220 --> 02:24.540
<i>Forbidden\h\h\h
</i>Deductions

03:38.990 --> 03:44.450
<b>#09   The Case of the Observatory Murder (Part 3)</b>

03:44.880 --> 03:48.460
Thank you for gathering on such short 
notice in the middle of the night.

03:48.930 --> 03:53.130
I've called you here to arrest 
the murderer as quickly as possible.

03:53.130 --> 03:55.920
I ask for your understanding 
and cooperation.

03:56.470 --> 03:57.890
Did you say "arrest"?

03:57.890 --> 03:59.390
So you know who the culprit is?

04:01.010 --> 04:01.850
Yes.

04:02.590 --> 04:04.310
They're here in this room.

04:07.730 --> 04:08.940
No...

04:08.940 --> 04:10.650
Then it really is...

04:11.020 --> 04:12.440
One of us?

04:12.440 --> 04:14.070
Can you explain everything?

04:14.460 --> 04:16.280
Yes, of course.

04:16.800 --> 04:19.240
I'll start with the incident 
that just occurred.

04:20.000 --> 04:22.530
After Grizzly-san was shot on the roof,

04:22.530 --> 04:26.350
Ron and I immediately rushed 
to the spot where he fell.

04:26.350 --> 04:29.870
Why? Because immediately 
following the rooftop gunshot,

04:29.870 --> 04:32.460
we saw him fall past the window.

04:34.410 --> 04:38.270
In other words, 
if we hadn't seen Grizzly-san fall,

04:38.270 --> 04:41.680
we naturally would've run up to the roof,
the source of the noise.

04:42.370 --> 04:47.520
But someone else ran outside 
to Grizzly-san first, too.

04:48.580 --> 04:51.600
And they came without an umbrella,

04:52.140 --> 04:55.880
all to disguise the fact that they'd
gotten wet on the rooftop

04:55.880 --> 04:57.570
when shooting Grizzly-san.

04:58.580 --> 05:00.280
The culprit...

05:04.480 --> 05:06.700
is you, Jumonji-san.

05:07.020 --> 05:08.460
The director?!

05:08.460 --> 05:10.840
Oh, come on. I would never!

05:10.840 --> 05:13.170
This is such a shock, 
I don't know what to do.

05:13.170 --> 05:15.750
You're jumping to conclusions, Isshiki-san.

05:16.130 --> 05:20.220
I was just so frightened that I mistakenly 
thought the gunshot came from outside!

05:23.990 --> 05:27.890
Besides, how do you explain Onodera-san?

05:27.890 --> 05:31.600
I was with you when she was killed, remember?

05:31.950 --> 05:34.060
I've already solved that trick.

05:35.980 --> 05:40.490
Jumonji-san, during the viewing party, 
you pretended to go back to your room.

05:40.490 --> 05:43.100
You then attacked Onodera-san, 
who was alone,

05:43.100 --> 05:45.240
and put her to sleep with medication.

05:45.970 --> 05:48.630
After that, you carried her to the dome,

05:48.630 --> 05:50.950
where you'd already shot out the lights

05:51.380 --> 05:55.170
and laid Ron, who you'd also put 
to sleep with the same medicine.

05:56.060 --> 06:00.080
That's likely when you put 
the master key in Ron's pocket.

06:00.450 --> 06:05.020
Then, as the finishing touch, 
you glued the doors shut

06:05.020 --> 06:06.990
and locked the two of them inside.

06:08.850 --> 06:11.860
Hang on! Then how did he lock the doors?

06:11.860 --> 06:15.260
We saw they were locked tight
when we had to break in here!

06:15.260 --> 06:18.520
Yes. That was the clever part of this trick.

06:19.880 --> 06:22.990
He gave Onodera-san a lighter dose than Ron.

06:22.990 --> 06:24.380
She woke up.

06:24.380 --> 06:27.320
First, she probably went for the light switch.

06:30.120 --> 06:34.270
But because the lights were broken,
they didn't turn on.

06:34.780 --> 06:37.680
What would Onodera-san do next?

06:42.230 --> 06:46.680
She would've noticed the doors beside 
the light switch and tried to get out,

06:46.680 --> 06:49.390
but they were glued shut and wouldn't open.

06:50.030 --> 06:52.760
In that moment, she would've 
assumed they were locked.

06:52.760 --> 06:54.350
She'd have turned the key,

06:54.350 --> 06:56.810
thinking she was unlocking them, 
but doing the opposite.

06:58.850 --> 07:00.510
There's no way...

07:00.510 --> 07:03.530
I mean, if I were in her shoes,
I would've done that.

07:03.990 --> 07:08.240
So you figured out the locked room trick! 
But there was a murder here!

07:08.240 --> 07:11.490
How could someone have shot her 
at that point, and who did it?!

07:14.160 --> 07:17.570
The perpetrator knew what 
Onodera-san's next move would be

07:17.570 --> 07:20.030
and set up one more trick.

07:20.030 --> 07:21.170
Another one?

07:21.980 --> 07:25.010
This fishing line that 
Grizzly-san left us is a clue.

07:25.640 --> 07:26.760
Fishing line?

07:27.490 --> 07:31.920
The culprit tied one end of the line 
to the top of the telescope,

07:31.920 --> 07:37.730
and the other to the trigger of a gun
 hidden and secured inside the air vent.

07:38.210 --> 07:42.260
Now, if the lights wouldn't turn on 
and the doors wouldn't open,

07:42.600 --> 07:45.360
where would Onodera-san go next?

07:46.200 --> 07:48.100
There, in the darkness,

07:48.510 --> 07:51.350
only one thing was illuminated 
other than the light switch...

07:51.350 --> 07:53.300
The switch to open the dome.

07:53.610 --> 07:56.490
With the ceiling open, 
starlight would fill the room,

07:56.490 --> 07:59.720
and if she shouted, someone might hear.

07:59.720 --> 08:02.090
Hopeful, she flipped the switch.

08:06.000 --> 08:07.650
But what happened then?

08:08.100 --> 08:09.470
As the dome opened,

08:09.470 --> 08:14.390
the telescope moved to record the star 
it had been preprogrammed to follow.

08:14.800 --> 08:16.050
It began to turn,

08:16.050 --> 08:19.290
pulling the attached fishing line taught...

08:21.590 --> 08:23.520
Until it triggered the gun.

08:26.160 --> 08:28.200
The bullet went right through Onodera-san!

08:29.860 --> 08:30.700
Star!

08:31.740 --> 08:33.890
The line Grizzly-san was holding

08:33.890 --> 08:37.550
was a piece that had snapped
when the telescope rotated.

08:38.210 --> 08:43.170
B-But the gun was on the ground next 
to Kamonohashi-san! It wasn't in the vent!

08:43.580 --> 08:47.660
The gun found next to Ron 
was the model from the lobby.

08:48.370 --> 08:52.700
As for the real gun, while we rushed over 
to the body and were all distracted,

08:52.700 --> 08:55.100
you retrieved it from the vent.

08:55.410 --> 08:57.880
Then you used it to kill Grizzly-san, too.

09:05.680 --> 09:07.840
Just wait.

09:07.840 --> 09:11.440
For the sake of argument, let's say 
that's how the murder was committed.

09:11.440 --> 09:13.360
But why would I kill anyone?

09:13.360 --> 09:15.830
Where's the proof that it was me?!

09:16.200 --> 09:18.790
I'm the one asking the questions here.

09:19.240 --> 09:21.360
Before you helped break down the door,

09:21.360 --> 09:26.580
before we'd even been in the dome, 
you asked Unno-san to get flashlights.

09:27.090 --> 09:30.050
How did you know that 
the lights inside wouldn't work?

09:30.050 --> 09:31.540
They were broken!

09:31.540 --> 09:34.730
And only the person who'd 
set this up would've known!

09:38.400 --> 09:39.310
Tch.

09:40.690 --> 09:42.270
Dear, oh dear.

09:42.730 --> 09:44.950
If you've seen through all of that,

09:44.950 --> 09:47.230
then I've lost this gamble.

09:52.080 --> 09:54.250
But I don't regret what I've done.

09:54.250 --> 09:56.580
Onodera died because she deserved it!

09:57.020 --> 09:59.200
What did Onodera-san do?

09:59.200 --> 10:05.040
That woman kept sniffing around the murders 
that happened here ten years ago!

10:05.040 --> 10:06.000
What?

10:06.430 --> 10:09.320
The celestial photography 
stuff was just a cover.

10:09.320 --> 10:12.500
She was really a journalist 
specializing in unsolved cases.

10:12.500 --> 10:14.490
The only reason she approached me

10:14.490 --> 10:18.470
was to look into what happened ten years ago.
 I realized that immediately.

10:19.040 --> 10:20.660
And at the viewing party,

10:20.660 --> 10:24.440
she slipped out so she could 
rummage through my room!

10:24.810 --> 10:27.590
So the reason Onodera-kun had to die

10:27.590 --> 10:30.400
is because you have something to hide.

10:31.900 --> 10:33.820
Maybe it's that gun...

10:34.650 --> 10:35.780
That's right.

10:36.400 --> 10:39.710
It was the same gun used a decade ago.

10:39.710 --> 10:42.340
I've kept it hidden all this time!

10:43.250 --> 10:46.910
On that day, my dad,
the director at the time,

10:46.910 --> 10:52.210
used it to kill all the guests and staff, 
then himself!

10:52.670 --> 10:56.670
I was the first on the scene, 
and when I realized what had happened,

10:56.670 --> 10:58.680
I knew that his crime...

10:58.680 --> 11:01.140
no, the shame he'd wrought had to be concealed!

11:01.630 --> 11:03.240
How could you?

11:03.240 --> 11:04.810
So that's the truth.

11:05.180 --> 11:09.810
I only wanted to live 
the rest of my life in peace!

11:09.810 --> 11:13.490
But that stupid woman 
wanted to dig it all up!

11:13.490 --> 11:16.140
And Grizzly was the same kind of stupid!

11:16.140 --> 11:20.240
If he'd just thought Kamonohashi did it, 
everything would have been fine!

11:20.240 --> 11:23.960
If he hadn't stuck his nose where 
it didn't belong and ruined my peace,

11:23.960 --> 11:25.830
I'd have even paid him a hefty reward!

11:25.830 --> 11:28.210
What are you saying?

11:28.210 --> 11:29.600
Shoot yourself.

11:33.640 --> 11:36.680
Console the dead with your death.

11:37.970 --> 11:39.180
The gun's gone!

11:49.120 --> 11:50.940
No! Stop it, Ron!

11:55.620 --> 11:56.780
What did I do?

12:00.690 --> 12:04.260
I won't let you kill me, Kamonohashi-san.

12:04.260 --> 12:07.300
I'll handle my loose ends myself.

12:08.170 --> 12:09.290
Wait, what is that?

12:09.290 --> 12:10.320
Oh no!

12:14.340 --> 12:15.630
Spit it back up!

12:16.020 --> 12:17.920
It's too late!

12:19.010 --> 12:21.760
Hey! There are still things 
I want to ask you!

12:21.760 --> 12:23.250
Why did you choose me?

12:23.250 --> 12:27.110
Is there a reason it was me
and not someone else?

12:27.110 --> 12:29.780
Was my coming here all part of your plan?

12:30.210 --> 12:31.810
O-Of course it was.

12:34.340 --> 12:39.950
No matter how much you struggle... 
you're still dancing in that person's palm.

12:39.950 --> 12:42.910
What does that mean? 
Who are you talking about?

12:45.020 --> 12:47.310
Night turns to dawn...

12:48.870 --> 12:50.330
Don't die, Jumonji!

12:50.330 --> 12:53.020
Answer me! I still have questions!

12:53.020 --> 12:54.530
Hey, Jumonji!

12:54.530 --> 12:55.800
R-Ron...

13:06.340 --> 13:08.100
His pupils are dilated.

13:08.920 --> 13:12.060
It's done. I'm sorry to say it, but he's dead.

13:12.490 --> 13:15.020
This almond smell... 
Was it potassium cyanide?

13:28.700 --> 13:31.410
Okay. We'll be waiting.

13:32.760 --> 13:35.630
The local police say they're on their way.

13:35.630 --> 13:37.680
What took them so long?

13:37.680 --> 13:39.170
That's a relief, star!

13:39.170 --> 13:41.590
These tears show no sign of stopping.

13:47.490 --> 13:50.520
So, it was all part of the plan 
from the very beginning?

13:51.250 --> 13:53.460
You used my love of black sugar syrup

13:53.460 --> 13:56.780
and invited me to the 
viewing party through Toto.

13:56.780 --> 14:01.200
You set it up to look like I'd committed 
murder in front of a BLUE instructor

14:01.200 --> 14:02.490
and trapped me.

14:03.170 --> 14:06.960
To manage all of that... 
Who were you really?

14:06.960 --> 14:10.200
If you did it all at someone else's
 behest, then who?

14:19.160 --> 14:23.050
An observatory director's last words
were "night turns to dawn"...

14:23.050 --> 14:24.720
That was quite tastefully done.

14:30.500 --> 14:32.310
Look. Dawn is here.

14:51.260 --> 14:52.330
Ron!

14:52.790 --> 14:54.780
The local police are here.

14:55.400 --> 14:56.540
I see.

15:13.670 --> 15:15.270
Excuse me...

15:23.190 --> 15:26.580
That wraps up the questions,
 Orihime-san. Thank you.

15:26.580 --> 15:27.730
Isshiki-san!

15:27.730 --> 15:28.490
Yes?

15:28.490 --> 15:32.450
When you're working, 
you're a sparkling first-magnitude star!

15:32.450 --> 15:35.620
Huh? First magnitude?

15:36.400 --> 15:38.430
Comet Dash!

15:38.430 --> 15:40.310
S-S-S-Star!

15:43.650 --> 15:47.260
They retrieved the bodies 
and the police boat has departed.

15:47.260 --> 15:50.260
We can leave whenever we're ready.

15:51.120 --> 15:55.730
I have regrets. To think we'd be sending 
Instructor Grizzly back in a bag...

15:56.280 --> 15:57.170
Yeah...

15:57.170 --> 16:00.690
He was a man who might've understood me.

16:02.820 --> 16:03.750
Toto.

16:04.600 --> 16:05.860
Do you remember?

16:05.860 --> 16:10.490
Before we came to this island, 
I said I was done sleuthing.

16:10.490 --> 16:11.990
I'm taking that back.

16:12.950 --> 16:16.950
The fact that this incident 
so closely resembled my past

16:16.950 --> 16:18.510
was no coincidence.

16:18.510 --> 16:21.380
Your past? You mean 
the Bloody Training Incident?

16:21.780 --> 16:22.840
Yes.

16:23.200 --> 16:26.200
Just like in that murder case five years ago,

16:26.200 --> 16:30.100
I woke at the scene of the crime 
with no memory of it

16:30.100 --> 16:32.220
and was made the prime suspect.

16:33.440 --> 16:35.020
That's true...

16:35.020 --> 16:37.520
I found another point of similarity

16:37.910 --> 16:40.980
at the scene of Onodera-kun's murder, 
bathed in morning light...

16:45.820 --> 16:47.360
This mark!

16:47.360 --> 16:49.820
It's the same as the scar on your neck, Ron!

16:50.320 --> 16:51.840
It was dark the whole time.

16:51.840 --> 16:54.420
I didn't notice it at first
 on the black carpet,

16:54.420 --> 16:58.540
but it was drawn there in red ink 
before she was killed.

16:58.540 --> 17:00.470
Wh-What are you saying?

17:01.880 --> 17:03.960
I should have realized it sooner.

17:04.570 --> 17:07.890
If you look at my history objectively,

17:07.890 --> 17:10.720
the Bloody Training Incident 
was totally different.

17:11.110 --> 17:14.500
The perpetrators died 
and suspicion was cast on me.

17:14.500 --> 17:17.340
Nothing like it ever happened before
and hasn't again since.

17:18.210 --> 17:23.810
I only started pressuring culprits 
to death after that incident.

17:23.810 --> 17:27.360
And most important of all, 
that's how I got this scar.

17:29.130 --> 17:32.780
In other words, I was framed 
for the Bloody Training Incident!

17:32.780 --> 17:34.910
Framed? By who?

17:36.170 --> 17:38.200
Jumonji said something about <i>someone</i>...

17:39.220 --> 17:41.690
I'd devoted my life to deduction,

17:41.690 --> 17:44.920
and that <i>someone</i> stole five years 
of sleuthing from me!

17:45.700 --> 17:49.250
Whoever it is grew tired of waiting
 for me to realize it in my grief,

17:49.250 --> 17:53.340
so they very kindly cooked up a murder 
recreating elements from five years ago

17:53.340 --> 17:54.890
and invited me to it.

17:55.460 --> 18:00.600
It's like they're declaring that they 
possess brains far superior to mine...

18:00.600 --> 18:04.850
Like they're laughing because they're holding
my life as a detective in their hands!

18:04.850 --> 18:08.320
They're playing games! 
This is the greatest humiliation of my life!

18:11.280 --> 18:13.730
I will never forgive them.

18:22.150 --> 18:25.990
It wound up just me
 and the dead on this boat.

18:33.340 --> 18:35.220
I barely managed to escape death.

18:35.220 --> 18:38.140
All thanks to you 
and that fool of a detective.

18:38.770 --> 18:43.350
Still, I never dreamed you
could fake a suicide this way.

18:43.720 --> 18:47.810
With this, no one doubted I was dead.

18:47.810 --> 18:53.260
You're quite the actor. 
On behalf of the family, I applaud you.

18:53.260 --> 18:54.780
I don't deserve such praise!

18:56.020 --> 19:00.400
I accomplished the murder unscathed. 
Now I can begin my new life

19:00.400 --> 19:05.750
because you all reached out to me
when Onodera was pestering me.

19:06.090 --> 19:08.240
Even now, it feels like a dream.

19:08.240 --> 19:12.740
The legendary House of M, the pinnacle
 of the criminal underworld, really exists!

19:12.740 --> 19:14.720
And before me stands one if its members!

19:15.360 --> 19:18.600
It's said that all crime
passes through the House of M,

19:18.600 --> 19:20.260
and that what they commit personally

19:20.260 --> 19:22.080
is guaranteed to go unsolved!

19:22.080 --> 19:24.680
They are the greatest family 
in the history of crime!

19:24.680 --> 19:28.560
Seems we're better-known that we thought.

19:28.560 --> 19:31.650
By the by, how was Kamonohashi Ron?

19:31.990 --> 19:33.860
I was meticulous in my observation!

19:33.860 --> 19:37.910
When he figured out that I was the culprit, 
he suddenly changed, just like you said!

19:38.190 --> 19:41.050
There was genuine murder in his eyes!

19:41.050 --> 19:44.540
If I hadn't faked my death, 
I know he would have killed—

19:48.820 --> 19:51.420
Hearing that is enough for me.

20:03.590 --> 20:05.350
Brother, it's finished.

20:10.210 --> 20:11.520
I see.

20:12.170 --> 20:16.310
<i>He said that Kamonohashi Ron 
tried to kill the culprit.</i>

20:17.710 --> 20:20.700
I saw Kamonohashi Ron for the first time.

20:21.670 --> 20:23.170
What did you think?

20:23.170 --> 20:25.160
<i>He's not like anyone in our family.</i>

20:25.670 --> 20:29.640
I don't care that he's the sixth generation
 of a detective who was our natural enemy.

20:31.030 --> 20:35.090
And the ninth generation 
from a certain someone else.

20:36.000 --> 20:39.550
Well, did he get my message
 from five years ago?

20:40.270 --> 20:43.260
When he saw the mark that matched his,
 he turned pale.

20:45.460 --> 20:47.770
He clearly doesn't know what it means.

20:49.050 --> 20:50.780
One day, he'll come to appreciate

20:50.780 --> 20:54.040
the blood that flows in him from our side.

20:56.390 --> 20:59.280
The ultimate detective, Sherlock Holmes,

20:59.600 --> 21:02.110
and the master of crime, James Moriarty...

21:02.770 --> 21:05.330
That man possesses the blood of both.

21:09.610 --> 21:10.870
Ow!

21:11.210 --> 21:12.380
Sorry, Toto.

21:12.380 --> 21:14.290
Don't start hula hooping out of nowhere!

21:14.290 --> 21:15.920
For some reason, I don't want to go.

21:15.920 --> 21:18.570
Your depression lasted all of a second, huh?

21:18.570 --> 21:19.820
After more thought,

21:19.820 --> 21:23.510
I feel like having a mystery 
attached to me is wonderful.

21:23.510 --> 21:25.470
Give it even more thought!

21:29.690 --> 21:30.880
Oh, right, Toto...

21:30.880 --> 21:33.200
I forgot to ask you the most important thing.

21:34.930 --> 21:38.320
Will you continue helping me?

21:38.320 --> 21:39.110
Huh?

21:41.370 --> 21:46.120
Well, without me around, you'd end up 
a murderer before you know it. Right?

21:47.320 --> 21:48.580
That's some big talk.

21:51.620 --> 21:55.550
Oh, Chef Unno gave me the black 
sugar syrup she won't be using.

21:55.550 --> 21:57.500
I've got three, so I'll give you one.

21:58.040 --> 22:00.970
It's your favorite. 
Don't put yourself out. I'm fine.

22:00.970 --> 22:03.190
Then give it to Amamiya-kun.

22:03.190 --> 22:04.930
That looks like motor fuel!

22:05.410 --> 22:09.140
Maybe I should pick out
 a souvenir for her instead...
